What Happens When a Secret Is Compromised?

Suppose this secret is leaked:

AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY

The security team's response should be:

Secret Compromised
        │
        ▼
Generate New Credential
        │
        ▼
Update Secret Store
        │
        ▼
Revoke Old Credential
        │
        ▼
Verify Pipelines Still Work

Notice what we don't do.

❌ Keep using it.

❌ Simply hide it better.

❌ Hope no one uses it.

Once a credential is considered compromised, it should be replaced.

This Process Is Called "Secret Rotation"

Secret Rotation means:

Replacing an existing credential with a new one and retiring the old credential before or immediately after it is compromised or expires.

Organizations rotate secrets because:

They may be exposed.
Employees leave the company.
Security policies require periodic rotation.
Credentials naturally expire.
