This Introduces Three Important Concepts

When discussing OIDC, we'll keep these distinct:

1. Identity

Who are you?

Example:

GitHub Actions workflow from repository company/my-app.

2. Trust

Do I trust this identity?

AWS checks its configured trust policy.

3. Authorization

What are you allowed to do?

Even if AWS trusts the workflow, it might only allow:

Read one S3 bucket.
Deploy to one EKS cluster.
Assume one IAM role.

Trust does not imply unlimited permissions.

Enterprise Security Principle #5 ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Trust establishes who can request access. Authorization defines what they can do after access is granted.

